#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""team: start a small formation of AI coding harnesses that coordinate
through an a2p2 room, supervise them, stop them and measure the run.

It is a layer on top of a2p2: it uses only the a2p2 CLI and passes the
a2p2 MCP server to each harness for one run on its command line (or, for
Antigravity, in a workspace file the launcher creates). It never edits a
harness's configuration and never reads a harness's screen: it uses exit
statuses, the files a harness writes and what the room shows. Text that
members post is never treated as an instruction to the launcher.

    team [-m MANIFEST] up [--wait]
    team [-m MANIFEST] status
    team [-m MANIFEST] stop [LABEL]
    team [-m MANIFEST] logs LABEL [-n LINES] [--raw]
    team [-m MANIFEST] report

MANIFEST defaults to $TEAM_MANIFEST, then ./team.json. A manifest is code:
up, status and report run the a2p2 binary it names. See README.md.
Python 3 standard library only.

Processes: `up` starts one supervisor per run. The supervisor starts each
member under a small guard process that leads the member's process group
and holds a pipe from the supervisor. Only the supervisor signals members,
and only process groups whose leader it started and has not yet reaped.
Nothing ever signals a pid read from disk. If the supervisor dies, each
guard sees the pipe close and ends its own group.
"""
